		DVB-S2X VL-SNR Modulator/Demodulator
		====================================

This is a C implementation of the DVB-S2X Very Low Signal-to-Noise Ratio
(VL-SNR) physical layer as specified in ETSI EN 302 307-2.  All 9 MODCODs
are implemented with standard-exact puncturing and shortening, covering
the operating range from -2 dB to -10 dB Es/N0.

The library provides a complete transmit and receive chain: FEC encoding
(BCH + LDPC with puncturing/shortening), pi/2-BPSK and QPSK modulation,
symbol spreading, pilot insertion, PL scrambling, RRC pulse shaping,
feed-forward symbol timing recovery, multi-frame carrier frequency
acquisition, pilot-aided phase tracking, and frame synchronization.

Both burst-mode (single frame per call) and continuous-mode (streaming
with persistent lock state) reception are supported.


Building
--------

	make			Build libdvbs2x_vlsnr.a
	make DEBUG=1		Debug build (-g -O0)
	make test		Build and run all tests
	make clean		Remove objects and binaries

Requirements: GCC with C11 support, libm.  No external dependencies.


Directory Layout
----------------

	include/		Public headers
	src/			Library source
	tables/			LDPC parity-check address tables
	test/			Test programs

The build produces a single static library: libdvbs2x_vlsnr.a


Supported MODCODs
-----------------

  Idx  Mod         Rate   FEC    Spread  User bits  RF threshold
  ---  ----------  -----  -----  ------  ---------  ------------
   1   QPSK        2/9    64800    no      14128       -3 dB
   2   pi/2-BPSK   1/5    32400    no       5580       -6 dB
   3   pi/2-BPSK   11/45  32400    no       7660       -5 dB
   4   pi/2-BPSK   1/3    32400    no      10540       -4 dB
   5   pi/2-BPSK   1/5    16200    x2       2432       -10 dB
   6   pi/2-BPSK   11/45  16200    x2       3712       -8 dB
   7   pi/2-BPSK   1/5    16200    no       2992       -6 dB
   8   pi/2-BPSK   4/15   16200    no       4072       -4 dB (*)
   9   pi/2-BPSK   1/3    16200    no       5152       -3 dB

(*) MODCOD 8 threshold is -5 dB at symbol level; the extra 1 dB
    loss at RF is from carrier recovery at low pilot density.

User bits = payload capacity per frame (excluding BB header).
Thresholds measured through the full RF chain: RRC pulse shaping,
timing offset 0.30 samples, frequency offset 1e-4 cycles/symbol,
phase offset 0.7 rad, and AWGN.  Criterion: error-free at the
stated Es/N0 (single frame, seed 42).

Puncturing and shortening are applied per ETSI EN 302 307-2:
MODCODs 2 and 5 use shortening (xs > 0), all MODCODs use
puncturing (xp > 0).  The transmitted frame is shorter than the
native LDPC codeword by xs + xp bits.


Signal Chain
------------

Transmitter:

	User data -> BB frame (with xs zero prefix) ->
	BCH encode -> LDPC encode ->
	shorten (remove xs info bits) ->
	puncture (remove xp parity bits, period P) ->
	bit interleave -> modulate (pi/2-BPSK or QPSK) ->
	symbol spread (MODCODs 5,6 only) ->
	PL frame assembly (PL header + WH header + pilots) ->
	PL scramble (data field only) -> RRC pulse shape

Receiver:

	RRC matched filter (persistent in streaming mode) ->
	Oerder-Meyr feed-forward timing recovery ->
	[AFC pre-correction (streaming mode only)] ->
	frame sync (segment-coherent WH correlation) ->
	AFC accumulator update ->
	coarse frequency (L&R, SNR-gated above 4 dB) ->
	residual carrier track (WH + pilot linear phase fit) ->
	PL descramble -> pilot extract -> despread ->
	soft demap (LLR) -> deinterleave ->
	depuncture (insert zero-LLR at punctured positions) ->
	deshorten (insert +40 LLR at shortened positions) ->
	LDPC decode (sum-product, 200 iterations max) ->
	BCH decode -> BB frame parse


Public API
----------

The public interface is defined in include/dvbs2x_vlsnr.h.  Link
against libdvbs2x_vlsnr.a and libm.

All functions return 0 on success, -1 on error unless noted.


0. Library initialization

	dvbs2x_library_init();

  Call once at program startup before any other API function.
  Initializes static lookup tables (LDPC box-plus LUT, VL-SNR
  header reference sequences).  Thread-safe operation requires
  this call to complete before spawning worker threads.

  If omitted, tables are initialized lazily on first use (safe
  for single-threaded programs).


1. Initialization

	#include "dvbs2x_vlsnr.h"

	struct dvbs2x_modulator mod;
	struct dvbs2x_demodulator demod;

	dvbs2x_modulator_init(&mod, modcod_idx, rolloff, sps,
			      scrambling_idx);
	dvbs2x_demodulator_init(&demod, rolloff, sps, scrambling_idx);

  modcod_idx	  MODCOD index, 1 through 9 (see table above).
  rolloff	  RRC roll-off factor.  0.35 is the DVB-S2X default.
  sps		  Samples per symbol.  Minimum 2.
  scrambling_idx  PL scrambling sequence index, 0-7.

  The demodulator allocates internal resources (LDPC CSR matrix,
  working memory).  Call dvbs2x_demodulator_destroy() when done.


2. Modulation (RF output)

	struct dvbs2x_complex *output;
	unsigned int out_len;

	output = malloc(cap * sizeof(struct dvbs2x_complex));
	dvbs2x_modulate(&mod, user_data, user_bits, output, &out_len);

  user_data	Input bit array (uint8_t, one bit per byte, 0/1).
  user_bits	Number of user data bits.  Maximum per frame:
		mc->k_bch - mc->xs - 80.
  output	Caller-allocated buffer for baseband IQ samples.
  out_len	Number of output samples produced.

  Buffer sizing (safe upper bound):

	unsigned int tx = dvbs2x_tx_coded_bits(mc);
	cap = (DVBS2X_PLHEADER_LEN + DVBS2X_VLSNR_HDR_LEN +
	       tx * 2 + (tx * 2 / 1440 + 1) * 36 + 64) * sps;


3. Modulation (symbol-rate output)

	dvbs2x_modulate_symbols(&mod, user_data, user_bits,
				symbols, &sym_len);

  Same as dvbs2x_modulate() but produces symbol-rate output
  without RRC pulse shaping.  Use when the DAC/SDR handles
  pulse shaping, or for symbol-level simulation.


4. Demodulation (burst mode, RF input)

	ret = dvbs2x_demodulate(&demod, input, in_len,
				user_out, &rec_len);

  input		Baseband IQ samples at the configured sps rate.
		Must contain at least one complete PL frame.
  in_len	Number of input samples.
  user_out	Decoded user data bits (one bit per byte).
  rec_len	Number of user bits recovered.

  Returns 0 on successful FEC decode, -1 otherwise.

  Each call is independent: the matched filter and timing
  recovery are reset.  The AFC accumulates across calls but
  does not apply pre-correction in burst mode.


5. Demodulation (burst mode, symbol-rate input)

	ret = dvbs2x_demodulate_symbols(&demod, symbols, sym_len,
					noise_var, user_out, &rec_len);

  noise_var	Per-component noise variance.  Pass 0.0 for the
		internal second-difference estimator.

  Symbol-level receiver core.  Use when timing recovery and
  matched filtering are handled externally.


6. Demodulation (streaming / continuous mode)

	ret = dvbs2x_demodulate_stream(&demod, input, in_len,
				       user_out, &rec_len, &consumed);

  consumed	Number of input samples consumed (caller advances
		its read pointer by this amount).

  Streaming receiver with persistent state across calls.  The
  matched filter delay line, AFC frequency estimate, and lock
  state carry over between frames.  State machine:

	SEARCH  -> first successful decode -> ACQUIRE
	ACQUIRE -> 3 consecutive successes -> TRACK
	TRACK   -> 3 consecutive failures  -> SEARCH

  In TRACK mode the receiver predicts frame boundaries from the
  known frame length, reducing acquisition overhead.

  Feed contiguous samples.  Returns 0 when a frame is decoded,
  -1 when no frame could be recovered from the current chunk.


7. MODCOD query

	const struct dvbs2x_modcod *mc;
	mc = dvbs2x_vlsnr_get_modcod(modcod_idx);

  Returns a pointer to the MODCOD parameter structure (1-9),
  or NULL if the index is out of range.

  Useful fields:
	mc->k_bch		BCH input capacity (bits)
	mc->xs			Shortening length
	mc->fec_len		LDPC codeword length
	mc->code_rate_num/den	Code rate fraction
	mc->has_spread		Spreading factor (0 or 1)

  User data capacity:  mc->k_bch - mc->xs - 80  bits.
  Transmitted coded bits:  dvbs2x_tx_coded_bits(mc).


8. Resource cleanup

	dvbs2x_modulator_destroy(&mod);
	dvbs2x_demodulator_destroy(&demod);

  Releases all resources held by the modulator/demodulator.
  The demodulator frees the cached LDPC parity-check matrix and
  pre-allocated decoder working memory.  The modulator destroy
  is currently a no-op but should be called for forward
  compatibility.  Both are safe to call multiple times.


9. Version query

	printf("libdvbs2x_vlsnr %s\n", dvbs2x_version_string());

  Returns "major.minor.patch" (currently "1.0.0").
  Compile-time macros: DVBS2X_VERSION_MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH.


Minimal Example
---------------

	#include "dvbs2x_vlsnr.h"
	#include <stdlib.h>

	int main(void)
	{
		struct dvbs2x_modulator mod;
		struct dvbs2x_demodulator demod;
		const struct dvbs2x_modcod *mc;
		struct dvbs2x_complex *iq;
		uint8_t *tx_data, *rx_data;
		unsigned int tx_bits, out_len, rx_len;
		unsigned int cap, i;

		dvbs2x_library_init();

		dvbs2x_modulator_init(&mod, 5, 0.35, 2, 0);
		dvbs2x_demodulator_init(&demod, 0.35, 2, 0);

		mc = dvbs2x_vlsnr_get_modcod(5);
		tx_bits = mc->k_bch - mc->xs - 80;

		tx_data = calloc(tx_bits, 1);
		rx_data = calloc(mc->k_bch, 1);
		cap = 80000;
		iq = calloc(cap, sizeof(*iq));

		for (i = 0; i < tx_bits; i++)
			tx_data[i] = i & 1;

		dvbs2x_modulate(&mod, tx_data, tx_bits, iq, &out_len);

		/* ... channel impairments ... */

		if (dvbs2x_demodulate(&demod, iq, out_len,
				      rx_data, &rx_len) == 0)
			/* success */;

		dvbs2x_demodulator_destroy(&demod);
		dvbs2x_modulator_destroy(&mod);
		free(tx_data);
		free(rx_data);
		free(iq);
		return 0;
	}

Compile:

	gcc -Iinclude -o example example.c -L. -ldvbs2x_vlsnr -lm


Test Programs
-------------

  test_modulator	Unit tests for individual blocks (BCH, LDPC,
			RRC, PL header, scrambler, modulation).

  test_loopback		Noiseless loopback for all 9 MODCODs.  Verifies
			the encode/decode chain produces zero errors.

  test_e2e		Modulator pipeline check.  Verifies frame
			lengths and RRC output for all MODCODs.

  test_api_loopback	Public API loopback with configurable
			impairments (freq, phase, timing, noise).
			Usage: test_api_loopback [modcod] [esn0]
			       [mode] [seed] [freq] [phase] [timing]

  test_ber		BER waterfall for a single MODCOD.
			Usage: test_ber [modcod] [frames_per_point]

  test_ber_vlsnr	LDPC-level BER with puncturing/shortening.

  test_rf_ber		Full RF chain BER for all 9 MODCODs.
			Usage: test_rf_ber [modcod] [frames_per_point]

  test_stream		Multi-frame streaming reception test.
			Usage: test_stream [modcod] [esn0] [frames]
			       [freq_offset]


Implementation Notes
--------------------

LDPC Decoder:

  Layered sum-product (belief propagation) with exact box-plus
  check-node update via a 512-entry precomputed LUT for the
  log1p(exp(-x)) correction term.  LLR values clamped to +/-40.
  Maximum 200 iterations (DVBS2X_LDPC_MAX_ITER), convergence
  checked every 5 iterations to reduce syndrome-check overhead.

  The parity-check matrix is built once at decoder initialization
  in Compressed Sparse Row (CSR) format and cached for reuse.
  All working memory (VN beliefs, edge messages, forward/backward
  buffers) is pre-allocated -- no heap allocation during decoding.

RRC Filter:

  Double-length linear delay line (mirror writes) eliminates the
  branch in the convolution inner loop, enabling compiler auto-
  vectorization.  The filter state persists across calls in
  streaming mode for seamless frame-boundary transitions.

Frame Synchronization:

  Segment-coherent Walsh-Hadamard correlation: the 896-symbol
  header is divided into 128-symbol segments, each correlated
  coherently, magnitudes summed across segments.  Tolerates
  residual frequency offsets up to ~2e-3 cycles/symbol.

  A minimum confidence threshold (0.05) gates processing to
  avoid wasting cycles on noise-only input.

Carrier Recovery:

  Three-layer approach:

  1. Multi-frame AFC: coherent accumulation of single-lag header
     correlations across frames (IIR, alpha=0.95).  Capture range
     +/- 0.5 cycles/symbol.  Active only in streaming mode.

  2. Single-frame coarse: Luise-Reggiannini estimator on the WH
     header, gated above 4 dB estimated Es/N0.

  3. Residual tracking: weighted linear fit of unwrapped phase
     from the header and all pilot blocks.  The 896-symbol header
     anchors the phase; pilots provide the frequency slope.

Timing Recovery:

  Feed-forward Oerder-Meyr (square-and-DFT) with precomputed
  cos/sin table and 4-point cubic (Catmull-Rom) interpolation.
  Non-data-aided, open-loop -- no symbol-slipping at low SNR.

Puncturing/Shortening:

  Per ETSI EN 302 307-2: xs information bits are set to zero in
  the BB frame (not transmitted, receiver inserts +40 LLR); xp
  parity bits are removed at positions i*p_period (receiver
  inserts zero LLR).  The interleaver and frame geometry operate
  on the post-puncture bit count (fec_len - xs - xp).


Limitations
-----------

  - The Walsh-Hadamard sequences are implementation-specific
    (PN-covered, rows 33/61/69/131/254/292/392/411/434).  They
    are not the exact sequences from ETSI EN 302 307-2 Table 18.
    The library is self-consistent (own mod <-> own demod) but
    may not interoperate with other implementations.

  - No ACM (Adaptive Coding and Modulation): the MODCOD is fixed
    per modulator instance.  Switching MODCODs mid-stream requires
    re-initialization.

  - Static lazy-initialized lookup tables (WH references, boxplus
    LUT) are not thread-safe.  Use one demodulator per thread, or
    call any API function once before spawning threads.

  - BB frame TS packet reassembly does not span frame boundaries
    (the syncd field is not tracked across frames).


References
----------

  ETSI EN 302 307-1 V1.4.1	DVB-S2 base standard
  ETSI EN 302 307-2 V1.3.1	DVB-S2X extensions (VL-SNR: 5.5.2)
  ETSI TR 102 376-1 V1.2.1	DVB-S2 implementation guidelines
  ETSI TR 102 376-2 V1.2.1	DVB-S2X implementation guidelines


